eam."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In his first Olympic event, " [:a {:href "/athletes/151233"} "Nicolas Gestin"] " (FRA), silver medalist at the 2023 World Championships, won the men’s canoe singles slalom in dominant fashion, with a margin of 5.48 seconds total time over " [:a {:href "/athletes/143126"} "Adam Burgess"] " (GBR) in second place. This was the fifth victory in this event for France, after " [:a {:href "/athletes/90175"} "Tony Estanguet"] " won in 2000, 2004, and 2012, and " [:a {:href "/athletes/133830"} "Denis Gargaud Chanut"] " won in 2016."] "\n\n" [:p {} [:a {:href "/athletes/135976"} "Matej Beňuš"] " (SVK) finished third for the bronze, his second Olympic medal, after finishing second in the event in 2016."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Bib"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Qualifying"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/151233"} "Nicolas Gestin"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FRA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/FRA.png"}] "FRA"]] [:td {} "88.78 (1)"] [:td {} "93.12 (1)"] [:td {} "91.36 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "7"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/143126"} "Adam Burgess"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GBR.png"}] "GBR"]] [:td {} "90.87 (2)"] [:td {} "97.21 (4)"] [:td {} "96.84 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "4"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/135976"} "Matej Beňuš"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/SVK"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-ali